Find the array of prime numbers $(a, b, c)$ satisfying conditions as follows:
(1) $a < b < c < 100$, where $a$, $b$, $c$ are all prime numbers;
(2) $a + 1$, $b + 1$, $c + 1$ constitute a geometric progression.

A.text:
Find the array of prime numbers $(a, b, c)$ satisfying conditions as follows:
(1) $a < b < c < 100$, where $a$, $b$, $c$ are all prime numbers;
(2) $a + b$, $b + c$, $c + a$ constitute a geometric progression.

B.text:
Find the array of prime numbers $(a, b, c)$ satisfying conditions as follows:
(1) $a < b < c < 100$, where $a$, $b$, $c$ are all prime numbers;
(2) $a - 1$, $b - 1$, $c - 1$ constitute a geometric progression.

C.text:
Find the array of prime numbers $(a, b, c)$ satisfying conditions as follows:
(1) $a < b < c < 100$, where $a$, $b$, $c$ are all prime numbers;
(2) $a + 1$, $b + 1$, $c + 1$ constitute a harmonic progression.

Determine, in each case, all real numbers $x$ such that:
a) $\sum_{k=1}^{2012} \lfloor kx \rfloor = 2012$;
b) $\sum_{k=1}^{2013} \lfloor kx \rfloor = 2013$.
